      ],
      "text": "**For a healthy adult, a short, easy ride looks reasonably okay—but I’d skip a hard or long workout.** The latest Kuching readings I found are around **API 66–74 (moderate)**, below Malaysia’s unhealthy threshold of 101. ([jerebu.com](https://www.jerebu.com/?utm_source=openai))\n\nIf you have asthma or heart/lung disease, are feeling unwell, or the haze looks or smells much worse where you are, play it safe and ride indoors instead. Malaysia’s Health Ministry advises people with asthma or irritation symptoms to avoid outdoor activity until the API is below 50. ([moh.gov.my](https://www.moh.gov.my/teras/info-kesihatan/jerebu/artikel-dan-panduan-pengguna-berkaitan-jerebu/kekal-aktif-walaupun-keadaan-berjerebu?utm_source=openai))\n\nCheck the live APIMS reading just before setting off, keep the pace gentle, and stop if you develop coughing, wheezing, chest tightness, or unusual breathlessness. Also, Kuching’s forecast calls for isolated rain tonight, so watch for wet roads. ([met.gov.my](https://www.met.gov.my/en/forecast/weather/district/Ds504/?utm_source=openai))",
